diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index d1e8d5f..2dd9ea3 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -84,6 +84,24 @@ The build is tested on Linux, MinGW, msys2 and MSVC.
 See `pyrowave-c-test` which unit tests the shared C API.
 That test also serves as a basic user guide for the API.
 
+With `BUILD_TESTING=ON` (the standalone default), `pyrowave-rate-control-test`
+checks the encoder's embedded bucket prefix-scan shader on a Vulkan device.
+It compares every bucket with a CPU inclusive scan, including asymmetric inputs
+and impulses at vector and workgroup-half boundaries. No window is created.
+
+```
+cmake --build build --target pyrowave-rate-control-test
+ctest --test-dir build -R pyrowave-rate-control --output-on-failure
+```
+
+The executable also accepts a compiled finalize shader for testing GLSL builds
+or an old module as a negative control:
+
+```
+glslangValidator --target-env vulkan1.1 -o finalize.spv shaders/analyze_rate_control_finalize.comp
+build/pyrowave-rate-control-test finalize.spv
+```
+
 `build-steamrt.sh` builds against the Sniper SDK and is also supported.
 
 #### Android standalone build
